<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7502"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 8:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Embersage has posted an interesting profile of BTK on the profile thread. <BR>I agree that the big letter T has some meaning to BTK and that he is probably a college dropout.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7502-->
<!--Post: 7652--><!--Time: 1108635394-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7652"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 2:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy_Leagurer, <BR>As you know, I am in concert with your assertion that BTK was motivated to send the Vicki Wegerle information primarily because of the book announcement. If no such announcement had been made, and never would be made in the future, do you believe that BTK would have otherwise died anonymously? &#40;I lean more toward his remaining silent.&#41; <BR> <BR>The BTK story is too big for this to work, but do you think that a hard-line tactic such as the following may have had at least a plausible chance of &#34;getting at&#34; BTK&#39;s ego and hence forcing his hand?  <BR> <BR>&#42; Via the media, accent on the print medium, BTK is told that he gets zero publicity - ever - unless he gives up specific information on other, possible victims. &#40;ie. <i>crucial</i> information; I know that any communication from BTK is good in a behavioral sense and there is a chance he may unknowingly give himself away - however, I don&#39;t like the odds that BTK will &#34;trip up&#34; one of these times, and in the end, his souvenirs and word games - another term for them is &#34;taunts&#34; - won&#39;t amount to a hill of beans, as he has no intention of being apprehended. Ergo, crucial information or BTK is history, whereafter he swiftly becomes a trivia question at best.&#41; <BR>&#42; To help this announcement along, keep Beattie&#39;s book in the news, the print medium especially, and also have a few erroneous &#34;excerpts&#34; deliberately printed; information BTK knows is inaccurate, and <i>knows that WPD knows that it&#39;s inaccurate.</i> I believe this would have forced BTK&#39;s ego to at least half-way comply. I don&#39;t believe they would cause BTK to go out and kill again; he can&#39;t get away with it now, this is the Information Age, people are sophisticated and who&#39;s to say he won&#39;t kill again, anyway? <BR> <BR>We both posit that it is unlikely that BTK will be captured. Be that as it may, what would be your advice as to the best way to try to &#34;reach&#34; BTK, if you had one opportunity to do so, via the media?   <BR> <BR>These are of course hypothetical but I&#39;m interested in your thoughts. Finally, after very carefully reading your profile, I have one quick but very specific question I&#39;d like to ask, but am not going to post it. <font color="0000ff">Ed, if Ivy_Leaguer permits it,</font> may I send <u>one</u>, just this once, e-mail to Ivy_Leaguer through the @catchbtk.com domain? It&#39;s a quick question, you can read it if you want to. As I&#39;m on AOL, I&#39;d gladly create a quick screen name for this but due to my opposition to the absurd Mr. X theory from the Zodiac site, whenever I&#39;ve posted my e-mail address I receive, within minutes, a barrage of rather sophisticated, albeit psychotic, missives. I&#39;m not exaggerating one bit.  But if the domain idea isn&#39;t kosher, cool. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7652-->
<!--Post: 7655--><!--Time: 1108637779-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7655"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 2:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If I may interject here, trying to force BTK to do anything will have only one effect. He is wanted for murder. Moreover he has spent as much time as he could killing them, for the sake of watching them die...sometimes twice. <BR> <BR>I think the young women in the city of Wichita are going to take exception to any suggestion of playing head games with him so we can fill in some blanks quicker.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7655-->
<!--Post: 7657--><!--Time: 1108645655-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7657"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 5:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Which is why I wrote, <i>These are of course hypothetical.</i> And <i>The BTK story is too big for this to work.</i> Clear enough, Comrade? <BR> <BR><i>I think the young women in the city of Wichita are going to take exception to any suggestion of playing head games with him so we can fill in some blanks quicker.</i> <BR>If this is true, the site should shut down. You obviously haven&#39;t read every theory, Messages to/from BTK and so forth. Go burn a book. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7657-->
