<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8019"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 1:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No need to blow a soft plug George, it was just a remark. There is a difference between discussing BTK and giving BTK the attention he wants, &#40;I&#39;m sure he expects it to be negative&#41; and trying to interfere with his work of art. Artists are notoriously quick, and hot tempered. <BR> <BR>My point was basically mean&#39;t to minimize the chance of making him feel that he must demonstrate his control of the situation by rash means. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8019-->
<!--Post: 8079--><!--Time: 1108859267-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8079"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 4:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie, really good profile that you wrote. I&#39;m having a hard time deciding whether or not BTK is a complete loner or if he has some kind of social life.  I think he must have some limited social life, perhaps even one or two lifelong &#34;friends&#34; ... people less intelligent than BTK, that BTK has groomed to see him as Mr. Nice and Normal, so that BTK can keep up appearances.  I think BTK is smart enough that he would see the need to look like an ok guy with at least one or two friends.  &#40;The reason I think this, is that I once knew someone extremely narcissistic, manipulative -- anyplace she moved, anywhere she had a job, she&#39;d find one person to single out as her new best friend -- always someone fat, not too bright, low self esteem, someone who would look up to her and believe whatever she said.  I could see BTK being like that. He might make the effort just to try to fit in.&#41; <BR> <BR>He&#39;s probably pretty smooth on a superficial level, so I think he probably finds some superficial excuses to get out and socialize and look like an ordinary Wichitan -- a stamp collectors club?  Camping or fishing group that gets together a few times a year?  Boy Scout leader?  If Scott Peterson could volunteer to read to the illiterate in Modesto, I think BTK might do something similarly &#34;altruistic&#34; to keep up appearances.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8079-->
<!--Post: 8080--><!--Time: 1108859335-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8080"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 4:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, who is ONS?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8080-->
<!--Post: 8081--><!--Time: 1108859808-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8081"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:rwmm@swbell.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 4:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Audrey - I don&#39;t know anybody that is a real narcissist. &#40;Some come real close though!&#41; Thanks for the insight - and I agree with you about finding some sort of &#34;sidekick&#34; that he could always feel superior to. He may discard them and maybe recycle them as he needs to? That would definitely fit and help keep up appearances.  <BR> <BR>Thanks - that makes good sense.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8081-->
<!--Post: 8094--><!--Time: 1108870644-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8094"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Audrey, I mean the UNSUB now called &#34;The Original Night Stalker.&#34; He was linked to the EAR &#40;East Area Rapist&#41;, hundreds of miles north, all locations in California, via DNA, years and years later. There is a thread dedicated to him in the General Discussion topic. <BR> <BR>He began with rapes, minimum of 48 and probably more, and was entitled the East Area Rapist &#40;EAR&#41;. He progressed to murder and was then called the  somewhat confusing &#34;Original Night Stalker&#34; &#40;ONS&#41; - this before the DNA connection. Confusing, as Richard Ramirez is popularly known as The Night Stalker, even though these two are polar opposites. Still, EAR/ONS as he is usually referred to, can be looked at, to a degree, when comparing a serial criminal with BTK <BR> <BR>Like BTK, EAR/ONS was able to go years between &#40;murder&#41; attacks. He &#40;EAR/ONS&#41; may well have been in prison, which is a belief held by many who know the case. However, all attempts to connect him with prison have failed. Including DNA. EAR/ONS breaks every behavioral and profiling mold, including the good-old-fashioned-detective point of view. I consider him dead, but that may be an unconscious wish. He is the most unique murder I&#39;ve ever read of and if still alive, the most dangerous. Actual police detectives who have been on the case even admit he is one-of-a-kind and unfathomably dangerous, IF alive. Below is a thread on this board. Take a listen to the link provided in the first post, which includes a taped call the &#40;at the time, rapist&#41; left on a potential victims answering machine in 1978. No foul language but not for the kids, either. <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/1/340.html?1108593644" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/1/340.html ?1108593644</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8094-->
<!--Post: 8095--><!--Time: 1108870805-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8095"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 7:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->NightDriver: If you happen to see my above post, please correct any inaccuracies, esp. whether the 1978 &#40;previous thought 1990 or 1991&#41; phone call from EAR was made to a <u>potential</u> victim or an <u>actual</u> rape victim. Thank you.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8095-->
<!--Post: 8099--><!--Time: 1108871974-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8099"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 7:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, I apologize for overracting. It was the &#34;young women of Wichita remark&#34; which stirred me up. In my opinion, the young women of Wichita are infinitely more likely to be victims of horrible auto accidents than be targeted by BTK. Moreover, if some of the possibles, along with a planned attack on Anna Williams was intended, then these victims fall into the category of &#34;young at heart.&#34; <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> Artists tend to be suicidal rather than homicidal but either is a violent act, certainly. BTK shows some artistic ability; this doesn&#39;t mean his house is covered with his own artwork or that he did quick-sketches of people. However, there is no proof he <i>didn&#39;t</i> skecth or paint for a living or for additional income. <BR> <BR>Once again, this brings me to a flea market connection. As a veteran of such places &#40;mostly in Maryland, a few huge ones in Pennsylvania&#41;. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t believe that BTK will kill again <i>unless</i> he fears he is in imminent danger of capture; in this case, he isn&#39;t going to attack a house - rather, he will shoot anyone he perceives is out to get him. His patience belies this belief, however in panic, all bets are definitely off! <BR> <BR>Are there flea markets in or near Wichita which were also there in, say 1972? There is no better place to buy untracable supplies, including firearms...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8099-->
<!--Post: 8101--><!--Time: 1108874097-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8101"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 8:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lily, I enjoyed your profile. What struck me most was the final point, &#34;guy next door&#34; observation. And his being recently retired, even though I think the book notice started the recent communication. &#40;The book along with retirement is just as likely, maybe even more likely. Good point.&#41; <BR> <BR>But the guy next door. That&#39;s exactly why he&#39;s at large. To that, I&#39;ll add, my opinion only, he doesn&#39;t reside in Wichita but in one of its suburbs. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8101-->
<!--Post: 8102--><!--Time: 1108876282-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8102"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:rwmm@swbell.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 9:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George - you may be right. I wish I knew more about the geography and culture of Wichita. Been there - but don&#39;t know it real well. I live in an area where suburban sprawl has taken over - and most people don&#39;t live in the city.  <BR> <BR>Darn those Wichitan BTK hunters...they have such a great advantage! Maybe you&#39;re one of them? <BR> <BR>IMO - he lived near the victims in the 70&#39;s. Maybe not still, but did then. Also, I think a combination of retirement &#40;lost his sense of power&#41; and the book &#40;someone else getting attention and glory for his work&#41; is what is fueling the recent communications. Think about how any of us would feel to have some &#34;newbie&#34; come in and take away our legacy? <BR> <BR>Aside from anything else - I very much appreciate your input on my profile &#40;IMO&#41;. I&#39;ve waited a while to post it and I appreciate all of the feedback from you, Audrey and others.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8102-->
<!--Post: 8115--><!--Time: 1108881803-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8115"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 10:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wish I had a chance to be one of the Wichita BTK hunter&#39;s. Even in Winter. Supposed to snow here tomorrow night and I&#39;m in Maryland, which usually has winters far more mild than Kansas. <BR> <BR>A pleasure to comment on your profile. I noticed the considerable amount of thought put into it while I was reading it. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8115-->
<!--Post: 8124--><!--Time: 1108896489-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8124"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 2:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No sweat George...it got me thinking anyway. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.psywarrior.com/index.html" target=_top>http://www.psywarrior.com/index.html</a> <BR> <BR>This is a cool site pertaining to psychological operations in the military. check out the Propaganda Planning and Disimformation pages especially.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.psywarrior.com/sog.html" target=_top>http://www.psywarrior.com/sog.html</a> <BR> <BR>The second link is one page of the first. About halfway down the page is a story about &#34;Operation Humidor&#34;. Read that and see if it reminds you of anyone/thing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8124-->
<!--Post: 8194--><!--Time: 1108971618-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8194"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 11:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The problem I have with linking BTK resuming his communications to Robert Beattie&#39;s book is why resume communicatimg months after the announcement of a yet unpublished book when back in 1998 John Douglas in his book called &#39;Obsession&#39; begans the book with the lead chapter about BTK called Motivation X&#39;? <BR> Why didn&#39;t he come out then to refute that or since he craves publicity to encourage peoople to read about him right or wrong? <BR>He waited too long after it became publc knowledge that Beattie was planning the book and there still is no release date or even a publisher to print and distribute it.  <BR>I don&#39;t think Beattie&#39;s book has anything to do with his resurfacing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8194-->
<!--Post: 8201--><!--Time: 1108977802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8201"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 1:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It could have been a traditional thing such as the shock of losing a loved one, etc., which caused BTK to re-emerge. It could also have been the book. It could have been both. It could have been neither. I go with the book because BTK is seven years older now than when Douglas&#39; book came out and Douglas&#39; book had one chapter based on BTK. Not an entire book. In 2004, it&#39;s possible LE deliberately saw to it that a book mention was made, to see whether or not it would rile BTK - and to see if he was still living. It did. And how! If you should read this, BTK, realize that a group of cops outsmarted you. You fell right into a feasible trap. They played you like a violin and without question you were the object of ridicule. You lost and you are very fallible. <BR> <BR>There is also the possibility that in 1998 BTK felt as if he&#39;d better keep off the radar screen because he had something to hide? Just a guess. Are there any unsolved crimes in Wichita from say 1997 or early 1998? By this late date I wouldn&#39;t expect to see as much bondage, although it&#39;s possible. I&#39;d look at attacks where women were killed in their residences, alone. While there may be other victims, the known hard facts indicate that BTK was capable of extended periods of inactivity. The only way to hope to get to BTK is to put figurative cross hairs on his ego and then play to it. There are certain things he&#39;ll respond to but it&#39;ll take an expert to decided these things are and how they should be carried out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8201-->
<!--Post: 8202--><!--Time: 1108979023-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8202"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 1:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have not read Douglas&#39;s Obsession, but surmise its similar to his others books, such as Mindhunter, The Anatomy of Motive and Journey into Darkness. Douglas tends to dedicate each chapter to a serial murderer, murderer, rapist or terrorist. It seems the first chapter would be dedicated to the BTK Strangler. The BTK Strangler series of murders can be found in numerous books discussing serial murder. It appears as a brief discussion or reference to his crimes. The unknown subject is not offended by this approach. Beattie&#39;s entire book is dedicated to the BTK Strangler. The unknown subject considers this offensive. He believes Beattie&#39;s version could be considered by the media, law enforcement and the public as the authority text on the subject. It seems the BTK Strangler does not believe Beattie is competent or the appropriate author of his criminal career. The list of chapters in an earlier correspondence is an attempt to undermine Beattie&#39;s and law enforcement&#39;s understanding of the BTK Strangler&#39;s case.  <BR> <BR>The other reasons suggested for the reemergence of the BTK Strangler do not seem convincing. He is enjoying greater leisure and most probably freedom from relatives and friends in the last year. A divorce, the death of a relative or friend or another personal trauma does not seem compelling for the unknown subject to resume dialogue with the media and police. Psychopaths tend to have little or no compassion for human life. He will never reveal the reason for his reemergence. It would reveal more information than he desires. It would also undermine his desire for control and domination of the situation.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8202-->
<!--Post: 8325--><!--Time: 1109054556-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8325"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy Leaguer, Bravo! <BR> <BR>I neglected to mention that in Mr. Douglas&#39; book, the BTK chapter, entitled &#34;Motivation X&#34; &#40;nice wordplay&#41;, has the Oteros names &#40;deliberately&#41; as &#34;Peterson&#34; or &#34;Anderson&#34; or something similar and places the locale of the attack on the East Coast, if memory serves.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8325-->
